    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup checklist before this workflow can run 1. Fill in real credentials for: Groq Account, HuggingFace Account, Qdrant Account, Cohere API, Slack Bot (each was created as a placeholder - open Credentials in n8n and add the real keys). 2. Set the Qdrant collection name in Retrieve Candidate Chunks (currently a placeholder). 3. Set a real Slack channel in Alert: Knowledge Gap (currently #knowledge-gaps placeholder) and invite the bot to it. 4. Create the Postgres logging table once (Neon credential is already wired): CREATE TABLE query_logs (id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY, session_id TEXT, question TEXT, outcome TEXT, confidence_score NUMERIC, citations JSONB, latency_ms INTEGER, execution_id TEXT, created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()); 5. Confidence threshold is 0.5 in Confidence Check - tune after running the eval set (PRD section 7). 6. Answer generation runs on Groq (Llama 3.3 70B) instead of Claude, and embeddings run on HuggingFace Inference instead of OpenAI, per your request to use Groq/HuggingFace access you already have. Groq/Llama may follow citation instructions less strictly than Claude did - re-run the eval set (PRD section 7) to confirm citation accuracy still holds before treating this as production-ready. 7. This is the query workflow only (PRD Milestone 2). Qdrant needs chunks in it before retrieval returns anything - populate it manually or build the ingestion workflow next (PRD Milestone 1).",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 5
